@startuml
title Life of an EIP-7002 withdrawal request
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5

start
:Contract reads the fee with a staticcall
(empty calldata, zero value);
if (Fee above the caller's limit?) then (yes)
  :Revert in the caller;
  stop
else (no)
endif
:Contract calls the queue with 56 bytes
pubkey (48) ++ amount (8, big-endian gwei)
and value = fee;
if (Input and value accepted?) then (no)
  :revert(0, 0)
nothing is queued;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:Queue stores CALLER, pubkey and amount,
emits LOG0 of the 76-byte record;
:End of block: client calls the contract
as SYSTEM_ADDRESS with empty calldata;
:Contract returns at most 16 records,
updates excess, resets the block count;
:Client prepends type 0x01 and commits
the list in requests_hash;
:Consensus layer runs process_withdrawal_request;
if (Credentials, status and balance valid?) then (no)
  :Request dropped.
No error, no refund;
  stop
else (yes)
  :Exit or partial withdrawal scheduled;
  stop
endif
@enduml
